Subject: [PATCH 02375/11362] [outer-loop] ARC live-generalization gap:
 per-game internal-state RE does not transfer (design + gaps)

Operator asked whether the tn36 mechanic-cracking is being LEARNED for dynamic
application during LIVE submission on unseen games. Honest answer: NO. Captured the
assessment + the closing architecture as a durable design note + 2 gaps.

THE GAP (grounded in the code):
 1. The deep-RE solvers read INTERNAL state (env._game.fdksqlmpki...; 12 accesses in
    the tn36 solver) -- a live submission exposes ONLY rendered frames, so the
    COMPUTATION is non-transferable (banked click-trajectories still replay, but new
    unseen-game solving can't read internals).
 2. Manual LLM RE, not automated frame-only discovery.
 3. Per-game memorization, disconnected from the router/TRM stack (router knows only
    goal-distance heuristics; no mechanic-class awareness).

WHAT THE CLIMB WAS WORTH: the discovered mechanic TAXONOMY (translation+obstacles,
program-editor, transforms+collision, checkpoint-multirun, timed-traps) -- the input
to a generalization design, not a live solver.

THE BUILD: frame-only mechanic INDUCTION (extend E3 arc_executable_world_model) ->
mechanic-feature extraction -> learned STRATEGY router (extend arc_router from
heuristic- to strategy-selection) -> strategy over the induced model, closing into
BFS/DFS/TRM. Logged GAP-ARC-LIVE-FRAME-ONLY-INDUCTION + GAP-ARC-STRATEGY-ROUTER.
